.TH FSCK.INVFS 8 "2026-10" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fsck.invfs \- check an InvariantFS volume (fsck(8) front-end)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck.invfs
.RB [ \-a | \-p | \-y | \-n ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.RB [ \-C
.RI [ fd ]]
.RB [ \-t
.IR fstype ]
.I filesys
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsck.invfs
is the standard
.BR fsck (8)
entry point for fstype
.BR invfs .
It runs
.B invf-fsck
and translates its verdict to the exit codes boot tooling expects.
.PP
Only
.B \-y
repairs, by passing
.B \-\-fix
to
.BR invf-fsck ,
which still refuses every key range it cannot prove unreachable.
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-p ,
.B \-n
and the bare default never repair: a boot-time preen must not excise data.
.B \-\-discard-reachable
is refused outright; it destroys files and stays a manual
.B "invf-fsck \-f \-\-discard-reachable"
decision.
.B \-f
forces the (always full) check,
.B \-C
is accepted and ignored (no progress reporting),
.B \-V
prints versions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
no errors (includes MIRROR STALE: the tree is walkable, the mirror is
behind \(em a warning, not a boot-stopper)
.TP
.B 1
errors corrected (invf-fsck printed REPAIRED)
.TP
.B 4
errors left uncorrected (DAMAGED)
.TP
.B 8
operational error (cannot open or scan; repair refused on a DEGRADED volume)
.TP
.B 16
usage error
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-fsck (8),
.BR fsck (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
